01:15:10.780 --> 01:15:16.420
that would be a lot easier than just, like, clicking on each character and equipping just the things that you had already given them.

01:15:16.460 --> 01:15:21.040
But we saw that on Final Fantasy, so I think it deserves a pass here if it got a pass there.

01:15:21.980 --> 01:15:25.060
The mapping system, obviously, the biggest thing.

01:15:25.260 --> 01:15:27.880
But you can.

01:15:28.520 --> 01:15:30.100
We all have the internet now.

01:15:30.100 --> 01:15:31.280
You can just look that up.

01:15:32.320 --> 01:15:34.080
Uh, and I don't know.

01:15:34.240 --> 01:15:40.360
Like, for as difficult and lack of tutorials as it had, the manual did explain enough.

01:15:40.360 --> 01:15:48.040
And the difficulty curve is something that makes you play a little more cautiously, which is encouraged in a dungeon crawler game.

01:15:48.220 --> 01:15:53.960
What's the point of doing this if your party's just op and you can just steamroll every enemy?

01:15:53.960 --> 01:15:56.040
Like, there's a point to this being hard.

01:15:56.040 --> 01:16:05.160
So, the only other thing I'm going to add, and it's very controversial, but we've seen that games can have it, uh, even on the NES slash Famicom.

01:16:05.740 --> 01:16:08.480
I could have used, like, some kind of auto battle.

01:16:11.080 --> 01:16:18.960
Not even just because, like, most things were fight, fight, fight, parry, parry, parry, that I didn't feel like I really even needed to be involved in those.

01:16:18.960 --> 01:16:22.320
Uh, so I'm not asking for, like, less combat.

01:16:22.400 --> 01:16:30.620
I'm asking for just the ability to auto battle my way through that or kind of macro assign, uh, what I want my classes to do.

01:16:30.840 --> 01:16:33.160
Especially if they're just going to die in the long run anyway.

01:16:33.400 --> 01:16:36.540
It's like, I shouldn't have to actively be playing as them all.

01:16:36.640 --> 01:16:38.460
Because, again, I'm just the god that created them.

01:16:38.560 --> 01:16:39.720
I'm not their brains.

01:16:40.400 --> 01:16:42.460
So, it's not on the essential games list.

01:16:42.460 --> 01:16:44.480
